            "target_entity_instance": "Mielke skill",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "At the global scale, ShoreFor achieves a Mielke skill of 0.26, similar to our best- performing evolved model Global-1 (0.25). The consistent performance of ShoreFor across different point clusters suggests that wave energy is a significant driver of shore- line change globally, which is corroborated by our evolved models where wave power appears in all four presented models. However, on a monthly scale, we observe that wave-based evolved models show similar performance to ShoreFor in wave-dominated regions, while models incorporating sea level and freshwater drivers show improved performance in regions where these processes dominate. A more direct compari- son would require daily-scale data and models that incorporate the same physical processes, which is an area for future work.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "satellite altimetry (SSALTO/DUACS)",
