            "target_entity_instance": "regional sea level (SLA)",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Multiple techniques were used to derive the shoreline change drivers' time series. These methods range from satellite altimetry (SSALTO/DUACS) to detect daily regional sea level (SLA) [56], combined with atmospheric effects (winds and pressure, modeled with MOG2D, [57]), to climate reanalysis (ERA5, [58]) providing 3-hourly wave conditions (i.e. here bulk parameters significant height Hs and peak period Tp were used), and land surface model simulations (ISBA-CTRIP, [59]) for daily terrestrial freshwater runoff.",
